eated_at":"2026-10-21T04:56:04Z"},{"id":"17777774676","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":47482959,"login":"Master0K7","display_login":"Master0K7","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Master0K7","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47482959?"},"repo":{"id":1424613188,"name":"humblemuzzu/dumbtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:49:42Z"},{"id":"17777494980","type":"IssuesEvent","actor":{"id":246660215,"login":"jt-at-home","display_login":"jt-at-home","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246660215?"},"repo":{"id":1424613188,"name":"humblemuzzu/dumbtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv"},"payload":{"action":"opened","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57/events","html_url":"https://github.com/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57","id":5954491929,"node_id":"I_kwDOVOnfRM8AAAABYupWGQ","number":57,"title":"[device] Amazon Fire TV AFTCU9343B (Hisense-built 2025, Fire OS on Android 14)","user":{"login":"jt-at-home","id":246660215,"node_id":"U_kgDODrO8dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246660215?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home","html_url":"https://github.com/jt-at-home","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jt-at-home/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:45:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T04:50:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Brand\n\nHisense\n\n### Model\n\nAFTCU9343B\n\n### OS and version\n\nFire OS on Android 14\n\n### How did you enable developer mode and ADB?\n\nSettings > About\n\n### Where does the TV show its IP address?\n\nSettings > Network > Ethernet > Status\n\n### Which dialogs blocked automation, and what dismissed them?\n\nAllow ADB connection.\n\n### Anything surprising the next person should know?\n\nPartial success.  Used DeepSeek v41-flash in the Deepseek Harness.  This was the summary...\n\nThe launcher half is not possible on this TV\nYour set is an Amazon Fire TV AFTCU9343B (Hisense-built, Fire OS on Android 14). Fire OS keeps Home on the privileged com.amazon.tv.launcher (HOME priority 950) and ignores cmd package set-home-activity. A sideloaded launcher can be opened by hand, but it cannot take the Home button. So the Apple-TV-style home — dock, glass highlight, Inputs/Wi-Fi/Settings pills, Outfit clock — cannot be installed as Home on this device. There is therefore no build-and-install script and no dock order or wallpaper to change.\n\nWhat I could do — and did — is the debloat half.\n\nWhat is disabled\n35 packages disabled in four batches, with a reboot and app check after each:\n\nTelemetry/analytics — Amazon metrics, Ceviche, Diode, crash/log managers, ad ID.\nLauncher ads/promos/preloads — Blackbird ad sync, recommendations, demo content, easy-upgrade, Luna, miniTV, Silk, website launcher, local gallery, Help, legal notices, retail demo.\nAlexa/voice and casting — Vizzini, Aria, Cardinal, Alexa media/directive/alerts, RTC, DIAL, Miracast.\nUnused streaming — Netflix, Freeview, AirPlay, USB Media Player.\npm list packages -d after the final reboot shows 35: the two tuner inputs that were already disabled at purchase plus 33 from this pass. Fire OS re-enables com.amazon.vizzini and com.netflix.ninja at every boot; they are recorded in the list header rather than re-disabled after each boot.\n\nKept deliberately: the Amazon account/messaging/AppStore stack, Prime Video, YouTube, YouTube TV, Amazon Music, automatic firmware updates, Bluetooth/remote pairing, the keyboard, Settings, and all MediaTek HDMI/tuner inputs.\n\nThe boot hang — my mistake\nThe first pass disabled com.amazon.device.messaging, which is load-bearing on Fire OS. The TV hung on the boot animation; recovery reboot and cache wipe did not fix it, and the factory reset was the only way out. The second pass excluded device.messaging, tcomm, aca, dha2, rdmapplication and hedwig, and rebooted after every group. I’m sorry for the reset and the setup work it cost you.\n\nVerified after the final reboot\nHome comes up; YouTube, YouTube TV, Prime Video and Amazon Music all launch.\nThe remote’s Settings/gear key opens the quick settings panel with Channel Guide, Inputs, Display Mirroring and Sleep Timer.\ndumpsys tv_input still lists the HDMI, analog and ATSC inputs.\nNo new crash-buffer entries.\nThe stock launcher still draws its sponsored hero, “Sponsored” row, Disney+ promo icon and Netflix button; those are part of the launcher and cannot be removed without replacing it. Settings → Preferences → Featured Content reduces some of it.\n\nFirst attempt wiped to much and I had to manually factory reset, reinstall my apps.  After that I tried again and my AI identified the issue (mentioned above) and on the second attempt only the de-bloat stuff worked. The home screen change could not be implemented.\n\n### How far did you get?\n\nPartly worked\n\n### Confirm\n\n- [x] No IP address, MAC address, serial number, Wi-Fi name or account email is included\n- [x] I am fine with this being published under CC BY-SA 4.0","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv/issues/57/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:45:06Z"},{"id":"17777074662","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":19738301,"login":"Entepotenz","display_login":"Entepotenz","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Entepotenz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19738301?"},"repo":{"id":1424613188,"name":"humblemuzzu/dumbtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:37:58Z"},{"id":"17776726591","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":736221,"login":"sigra","display_login":"sigra","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigra","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/736221?"},"repo":{"id":1424613188,"name":"humblemuzzu/dumbtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/humblemuzzu/dumbtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:31:10Z"},{"id":"17776348159","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":113971627,"login":"chimt4chi","display_login":"chimt4chi","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chimt4chi","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113971627?"},"repo":{"id":1424613188,"name":"humblemuzzu/dumbtv",